    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">How Do You Pay for a Private Boat Trip in Madeira?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>22 December 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">On chifbay.com you pay online by card when you book, one price for the whole boat: 400 or 500 EUR for the Sunset Trip, 500 or 600 EUR for the Day Trip. If you book through GetYourGuide, Viator or Click&amp;Boat you pay the platform, and a custom trip, deposit included, is agreed on WhatsApp.</p>

      <h2>What exactly are you paying for?</h2><p>The whole boat, for your group only, for the length of trip you choose. Up to five guests, and the price does not move whether two of you come or five.</p><p>That one price buys the trip and all that comes with it: food and drink on board, poncha and beer and soft drinks and wine made on the island, a bathroom, a 360° recording of the day, footage from the drone whenever conditions let it fly, and real camera photos. For the Day Trip, add both swims and the paddle boards. There is no bar bill and no extras menu, so there is nothing to pay once you step off the pontoon.</p><h2>How much is it each if you split it?</h2><p>Simple division, because the boat is priced as one. Often one person pays with one card and the group settles up later.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Trip</th><th>Price per boat (EUR)</th><th>Each, 2 guests</th><th>Each, 3 guests</th><th>Each, 4 guests</th><th>Each, 5 guests</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sunset Trip, 2h</td><td>400</td><td>200</td><td>about 133</td><td>100</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>Sunset Trip, 2h30</td><td>500</td><td>250</td><td>about 167</td><td>125</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>Day Trip, 2h30</td><td>500</td><td>250</td><td>about 167</td><td>125</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>Day Trip, 3h</td><td>600</td><td>300</td><td>200</td><td>150</td><td>120</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Those are the only prices. There is no discount code to hunt for and no surcharge for a full boat.</p><h2>How does paying on our own website work?</h2><p>In a few steps, all online, before the day. You never hand over money on the pontoon.</p><ol><li><strong>Choose the trip and the date.</strong> The <a href="/hidden-coves-half-day">Day Trip with swim stops</a> leaves at 10:00 or 14:00. For the <a href="/sunset-cruise">Sunset Trip</a>, the booking page shows the exact departure for the evening you pick, since it follows the sun.</li><li><strong>Enter the lead guest's details.</strong> A name, an email and a WhatsApp number, so the skipper can reach you on the day.</li><li><strong>Pay by card.</strong> The payment runs through Stripe, a large payment provider, and Chifbay never sees or stores your full card number.</li><li><strong>Wait for the confirmation.</strong> Under the terms, the booking is confirmed once you receive it from us. Keep it on your phone.</li><li><strong>Turn up.</strong> Arrive at Marina do Funchal fifteen minutes ahead of departure, where the skipper waits for you. That last step costs nothing.</li></ol><h2>What if your card is not in euros?</h2><p>Prices are in euros, so a card in pounds, dollars or any other currency is converted by your own bank. Some banks add a foreign transaction fee on top of the exchange rate, others do not. If you are unsure, check your bank's app before you pay. The price per boat stays the same, only the amount on your statement changes with the rate.</p><h2>How does it work on GetYourGuide, Viator or Click&amp;Boat?</h2><p>You pay the platform, in the ways it accepts, and the platform pays the operator. The boat, the skippers, the route and what is included are the same as a direct booking.</p><ul><li><strong>Who you pay.</strong> The platform takes the money at checkout, or later if the listing allows it.</li><li><strong>Pay later options.</strong> GetYourGuide and Viator both offer reserve now, pay later on some listings. On Viator the card is charged automatically on a date shown in your booking, not at checkout.</li><li><strong>Extra fees.</strong> Click&amp;Boat adds a service fee to the rental price. Look at the final total, not the headline.</li><li><strong>Refunds.</strong> Any refund goes back through the platform you paid, under its rules.</li></ul><p>If you are torn between booking routes, compare the final total for your whole group on each site at checkout. Our page on <a href="/posts/book-madeira-boat-trip-direct-or-getyourguide">booking direct or on GetYourGuide</a> sets out the other differences.</p><h2>How do custom trips and deposits work?</h2><p>A trip at another time of day, or something outside the two set trips, is arranged with us on WhatsApp. The time, the plan and the price are agreed in that conversation, and so is how you pay. Usually that means a deposit to hold the date, paid through a personal payment link we send you, with the details written down before you pay anything.</p><p>The New Year's Eve fireworks night on 31 December 2026 is a special case with its own page: see the <a href="/new-years-eve-fireworks-boat-madeira">fireworks boat night in Funchal</a> for how it works.</p><h2>Can you pay cash on the day?</h2><p>The standard trips are paid when you book, so there is nothing to settle at the marina. If paying online is a problem for you, ask on WhatsApp before booking rather than arriving with cash and hoping.</p><p>The one thing some guests do hand over in cash is a tip for the skipper at the end. It is entirely optional. Our guide on <a href="/posts/do-you-tip-the-skipper-on-a-boat-trip-in-madeira">tipping the skipper</a> explains what is normal in Portugal.</p><h2>What happens to your money if plans change?</h2><p>It depends on who changes them. If you cancel 24 hours or more before departure, it is free and you get the full amount back. Inside those last 24 hours, the terms leave room for no refund at all. When it is the skipper who calls the trip off for safety, you decide between rebooking and having it all returned.</p><p>On a direct booking, a refund goes back the way you paid. On a platform booking, it comes back through the platform.</p><h2>How do you avoid paying the wrong people?</h2><p>Pay only through a real checkout: chifbay.com, a platform you trust, or a payment link from a conversation you started yourself. Never type a card number into a chat message or an email, for any operator. A licensed operator in Portugal is listed in the national RNAAT register, and Chifbay's number is RNAAT n.º 305/2026. Our page on <a href="/posts/how-to-check-a-boat-tour-operator-in-madeira-is-licensed">how to check a boat tour operator is licensed</a> shows where to look.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is the price per person or per boat?</h3><p>Per boat. One price covers up to five guests, whether two of you come or five.</p><h3>When do you pay for a trip booked online?</h3><p>When you book, by card, on chifbay.com. Nothing more is paid at the marina.</p><h3>Is there anything extra to pay on board?</h3><p>No. Food and drink, the bathroom, the 360° recording, the drone shots and the photos are part of the price.</p><h3>How do you pay for a custom private trip?</h3><p>It is agreed on WhatsApp, including a deposit to hold the date, paid through a personal payment link.</p>

      <blockquote>One boat, one price, paid once. How your group splits it is up to you.</blockquote>
    </article>
    <p class="pref-src" data-pref-source><span>Enjoying our Madeira guides?</span> <a href="https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=chifbay.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#4285F4" d="M23.5 12.3c0-.8-.1-1.6-.2-2.3H12v4.5h6.5a5.6 5.6 0 0 1-2.4 3.6v3h3.9c2.2-2.1 3.5-5.1 3.5-8.8z"/><path fill="#34A853" d="M12 24c3.2 0 6-1.1 7.9-2.9l-3.9-3c-1.1.7-2.4 1.2-4 1.2-3.1 0-5.7-2.1-6.6-4.9h-4v3.1A12 12 0 0 0 12 24z"/><path fill="#FBBC05" d="M5.4 14.4a7.2 7.2 0 0 1 0-4.7V6.6h-4a12 12 0 0 0 0 10.8l4-3z"/><path fill="#EA4335" d="M12 4.8c1.7 0 3.3.6 4.6 1.8l3.4-3.4A12 12 0 0 0 1.4 6.6l4 3.1C6.3 6.9 8.9 4.8 12 4.8z"/></svg>Add Chifbay as a preferred source on Google</a></p>

